# The seeded skill-library fixture is hashed byte-for-byte: its SHA-256 is real evidence rendered
# in the UI (apps/web/src/library-seed.ts). Git must never normalise its line endings, or the
# digest would differ between a Windows checkout and Linux CI and the displayed evidence would be
# wrong on one of them. Treat everything under apps/web/fixtures/ as binary-exact.
apps/web/fixtures/** -text

# Same reasoning for the two seeded Agent Skill fixtures (PR 2/4, ADR-017): their canonical
# package SHA-256 is real evidence rendered in the UI and pinned in
# apps/web/test/library-seed-fixtures.test.ts. The committed blobs are LF; without this, Git
# hands a Windows checkout CRLF and the digest silently differs from Linux CI and production.
examples/agent-skills/** -text
